WEBVTT

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:09.110
<i>Seeking greater power, 
I induced my own reincarnation.</i>

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:11.840
<i>Thousands of years later,</i>

00:00:12.260 --> 00:00:16.280
<i>I was reborn as Matthias, 
third son of the Hildesheimer family.</i>

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:24.670
<i>But when I finally regained 
the memories of my past life,</i>

00:00:24.970 --> 00:00:28.270
<i>I found myself in a world in which 
the strongest crest was decried as the weakest,</i>

00:00:28.790 --> 00:00:31.590
<i>and spellcasting techniques were in decline.</i>

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:06.980
<b>Episode 2</b>

00:02:02.510 --> 00:02:06.980
<b>The Strongest Sage Enters the Dungeon.</b>

00:02:07.760 --> 00:02:09.120
Don't touch the body!

00:02:09.120 --> 00:02:11.540
It could be booby-trapped!

00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:14.470
Say nothing of this, any of you!

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.360
Matty!

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:19.460
I'm so glad you're safe!

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:20.780
You weren't harmed, were you?

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.800
W-Well...

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:24.740
Say, Lurie.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:27.380
You know what you're doing, don't you?

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:30.370
Oh, what was I thinking?

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:37.020
Beating one demon 
really isn't that big a deal.

00:02:37.020 --> 00:02:40.510
No one in history 
has ever single-handedly dispatched a demon!

00:02:41.750 --> 00:02:42.970
Please, enter.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:49.480
Eduard. It has been some time.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:52.800
I am honored to be 
in your presence again, Your Majesty.

00:02:54.100 --> 00:02:58.320
We know each other too well 
for such formality, don't we?

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:00.870
Is that the boy?

00:03:00.870 --> 00:03:01.830
Yes, my lord.

00:03:01.830 --> 00:03:04.660
The hero of the moment, Matthias!

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:07.640
Currently in my first year 
at Second Academy's primary school,

00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.620
I am Matthias Hildesheimer.

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.170
I see.

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:14.400
I am duly impressed 
by your defeat of that demon.

00:03:14.400 --> 00:03:16.760
Under normal circumstances, I would send word 
of your meritorious deed far and wide

00:03:16.760 --> 00:03:19.320
and grant you a fief...

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:21.280
<i>No, not a fief! Anything but that!</i>

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:23.040
<i>I reincarnated to get stronger!</i>

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.340
<i>I don't want to waste my time 
managing a bunch of land!</i>

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:28.670
Unfortunately, a public proclamation 
would make it known

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:31.420
that demons have infiltrated our ranks.

00:03:31.420 --> 00:03:33.160
It could stir mass panic.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.440
I'll gladly take something else!

00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:38.840
A magic sword, perhaps?

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:42.280
I recently received a magic sword 
with a double enchantment.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:43.770
"A double enchantment"?

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:49.890
The blacksmith who sold it to me said 
it was enchanted by a passing child.

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:54.790
<i>Right, that store owner had me 
make a spare...</i>

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:58.170
May I infer that 
you find this insufficient reward?

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:01.840
Is there anything else 
you might desire?

00:04:01.840 --> 00:04:05.230
<i>I guess I'd better go for broke.</i>

00:04:05.230 --> 00:04:10.710
I request rights to all resources 
found in the kingdom's dungeons.

00:04:10.710 --> 00:04:12.900
The dungeons' resources?

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:16.560
Do you mean the ore that lies within them, 
and their monsters?

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:17.780
Yes.

00:04:17.780 --> 00:04:20.570
I'm not asking for a monopoly, of course.

00:04:21.390 --> 00:04:24.450
<i>Dungeons are a kingdom's greatest asset,</i>

00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:27.080
<i>superior even to high-quality gold mines.</i>

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:31.450
<i>In my past life, kingdoms would even go 
to war over dungeons,</i>

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:34.460
<i>and the monster parts 
and magical metals they contained.</i>

00:04:34.740 --> 00:04:38.440
<i>But magical knowledge has waned 
in this day and age.</i>

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:41.920
<i>It's entirely possible that they don't know 
the true worth of dungeons.</i>

00:04:41.920 --> 00:04:45.430
If that is your wish, 
then I grant you free rein.

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:48.390
You have my gratitude.

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:51.870
I shall consider the matter 
of your reward settled.

00:04:51.870 --> 00:04:54.550
Now, Matthias, 
I wish to hear your opinion.

00:04:54.550 --> 00:04:55.980
My opinion?

00:04:55.980 --> 00:04:57.220
Yes.

00:04:57.220 --> 00:05:03.820
The four magical chosen ones once present 
in this kingdom have all vanished.

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:09.690
This includes Erhard, 
last Captain of the Mages' Order.

00:05:09.690 --> 00:05:11.760
<i>The magical chosen ones...</i>

00:05:11.760 --> 00:05:13.080
<i>Demons?</i>

00:05:13.080 --> 00:05:18.420
Magical chosen ones first began 
to appear several hundred years ago.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:24.590
This suggests that demons have been infiltrating 
our kingdom for centuries.

00:05:25.730 --> 00:05:29.830
<i>In my past life, I drove the demons 
to the brink of destruction.</i>

00:05:29.830 --> 00:05:32.920
<i>But after I died 
to achieve my reincarnation,</i>

00:05:32.920 --> 00:05:35.910
<i>the few survivors 
must have infiltrated human society,</i>

00:05:35.910 --> 00:05:38.290
<i>spread erroneous magical knowledge,</i>

00:05:38.290 --> 00:05:43.110
<i>and caused human power to wane over time.</i>

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:47.740
It seems you have driven the demons 
from our kingdom.

00:05:47.740 --> 00:05:50.530
Does this mean 
the threat has passed?

00:05:50.530 --> 00:05:52.760
I fear not, Your Majesty.

00:05:52.760 --> 00:05:54.330
In fact, it may be more dire 
than ever!

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:56.870
What do you mean?

00:05:57.160 --> 00:06:01.730
If the unmasking caused 
the magical chosen ones to flee,

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:05.300
it's a sign that they see no value 
in maintaining the masquerade.

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:06.260
Are you saying...

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:08.800
The demons' next move may be 
to muster their forces

00:06:08.800 --> 00:06:11.040
and lay waste to this kingdom.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:15.280
That said, demons are not adept 
organizing en masse.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:19.250
If they intend to gather a great force 
before they attack us,

00:06:20.360 --> 00:06:23.210
I predict it will take them 
approximately three months.

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:26.030
A mere three months?!

00:06:26.570 --> 00:06:29.300
Hardly enough time.

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:30.460
It's more than enough!

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:35.120
We just need to cover the whole kingdom 
in a barrier before then.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.850
A kingdom-sized barrier?

00:06:36.850 --> 00:06:38.000
Yes.

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:42.490
We'll use a divine-class artifact 
to project a permanent barrier.

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:45.420
If all the students 
of Second Academy work together,

00:06:45.420 --> 00:06:47.760
we can finish the preparations in a month.

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:52.220
I advise that we continue teaching 
wordless magic in the meantime.

00:06:53.920 --> 00:06:56.890
We have no way of facing them ourselves.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:07:00.770
As you defeated a demon single-handedly, 
we must place our trust in you.

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:03.300
Matthias Hildesheimer...

00:07:03.300 --> 00:07:06.600
I appoint you leader 
of the fight against the demons!

00:07:07.740 --> 00:07:10.390
His Majesty said 
you could have anything you want,

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:13.870
for the creation of the barrier 
or otherwise.

00:07:15.900 --> 00:07:20.630
<i>For the magistones, mithril, 
and orichalcum I'll need for the barrier,</i>

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:23.510
<i>I might still have to hit up a dungeon.</i>

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:28.250
That was found in an ancient ruin.

00:07:28.250 --> 00:07:30.930
Unfortunately, no one knows how to use it.

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:36.230
<i>The pattern of the magic 
that runs through it...</i>

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:37.460
It is!

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:40.120
<i>It's a magic sword I made in my past life!</i>

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:44.690
<i>A test case from when I was obsessed 
with making magic swords.</i>

00:07:45.470 --> 00:07:47.210
I'll take this sword!

00:07:47.210 --> 00:07:50.110
Really? You'd like that sword?

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:53.450
<i>It's tougher than orichalcum.</i>

00:07:53.450 --> 00:07:56.200
<i>It'll be perfect for the barrier's core!</i>

00:07:56.580 --> 00:07:59.370
I'll also take this pendant.

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:02.330
<i>A magic accessory I made in my past life!</i>

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:07.170
<i>It vastly increases the gains 
granted by experience points.</i>

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:09.760
<i>It's precisely what I need right now!</i>

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:16.260
<i>They're starting to get the hang of it.</i>

00:08:16.800 --> 00:08:22.130
<i>I entreated the king for a reevaluation 
of casting theory and crest rankings,</i>

00:08:22.130 --> 00:08:25.680
<i>but it takes time for ideas 
to change once they've calcified.</i>

00:08:25.680 --> 00:08:28.330
<i>Still, I can't have humanity dying out</i>

00:08:28.330 --> 00:08:31.980
<i>before I can make myself properly strong.</i>

00:08:32.300 --> 00:08:34.700
<i>I'll need to work with them for a while.</i>

00:08:35.080 --> 00:08:36.340
Matty!

00:08:36.340 --> 00:08:38.440
The headmaster told us!

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:41.140
You're making a barrier 
to protect the kingdom?

00:08:41.140 --> 00:08:41.880
Yes.

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:45.460
I'll be heading to a dungeon 
to collect the materials needed.

00:08:45.730 --> 00:08:46.710
A dungeon?

00:08:46.710 --> 00:08:48.290
You're going in already?

00:08:48.560 --> 00:08:49.700
<i>That's right...</i>

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:54.100
<i>It's always better 
to have a party in dungeons.</i>

00:08:54.100 --> 00:08:55.510
Lurie, Alma...

00:08:56.480 --> 00:08:57.220
Yes?

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:00.320
W-Will you be...

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:04.180
Will you be my party?

00:09:04.180 --> 00:09:06.040
P-Party?

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:10.020
Go into the dungeon with you, 
you mean?

00:09:12.320 --> 00:09:16.730
<i>D-Do they not feel comfortable around me?</i>

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:19.490
We're thrilled by the invitation,

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:22.100
but are you certain 
we won't hold you back?

00:09:22.100 --> 00:09:24.370
I'd love to get stronger,

00:09:24.370 --> 00:09:27.030
but I'm not great with a sword.

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:30.020
You've always been better 
with a bow, haven't you?

00:09:30.020 --> 00:09:30.960
Yeah...

00:09:30.960 --> 00:09:33.140
And bows are great for hunting,

00:09:33.140 --> 00:09:37.300
but I was told they're bad for combat, 
since they don't play well with casting.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:39.920
Oh, is that all?

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:42.670
Bows are great for magical combat!

00:09:42.670 --> 00:09:44.140
They are?

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:47.490
Watch, Alma!

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:52.440
You infused the arrow with magic?

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:55.320
That was Simple Magic Enchant.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:56.650
That's incredible!

00:09:56.650 --> 00:09:58.370
In your hands, at least...

00:09:58.370 --> 00:10:00.180
I'm not sure I can measure up.

00:10:00.180 --> 00:10:03.410
I think you can.

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:06.040
Besides, you have the Crest of Standard.

00:10:06.040 --> 00:10:08.250
It's the ideal crest for magical archery.

00:10:08.510 --> 00:10:10.000
Really?

00:10:10.000 --> 00:10:13.570
Maybe I will join your party, then!

00:10:13.570 --> 00:10:16.530
Did you say that was an enchantment?

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:19.580
Yeah, of a sort. 
You're infusing an arrow with magical power.

00:10:19.580 --> 00:10:21.140
Can I do the same thing?!

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:22.100
Uh...

00:10:22.100 --> 00:10:24.510
Do you like casting enchantments, Lurie?

00:10:24.510 --> 00:10:25.470
Yes!

00:10:25.470 --> 00:10:28.700
Watching you do it piqued my interest!

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:32.220
And if I'm infusing equipment 
with magical power, I won't have to fight!

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:33.440
Oh, is that the reason?

00:10:33.910 --> 00:10:38.000
Your crest is better for enchantments 
than for combat, anyway.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.920
But that's wonderful!

00:10:39.920 --> 00:10:42.700
I would love to join your party, Matty!

00:10:42.700 --> 00:10:44.960
Teach me all there is to know 
about enchantments!

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:45.990
S-Sure...

00:10:46.680 --> 00:10:48.200
Lurie...

00:10:48.200 --> 00:10:50.170
Oh, there I go again...

00:10:50.590 --> 00:10:54.360
<i>She's so thrilled 
about the properties of the crest</i>

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:56.550
<i>that I reincarnated to be rid of.</i>

00:10:56.550 --> 00:10:58.670
<i>But now I'm ready to go.</i>

00:10:59.280 --> 00:11:03.120
<i>With my close-combat-specialized Fourth Crest, 
I can hold the front line,</i>

00:11:03.120 --> 00:11:05.730
<i>while Alma reinforces me from behind,</i>

00:11:05.730 --> 00:11:08.060
<i>and Lurie, with her First Crest, 
offers support.</i>

00:11:08.060 --> 00:11:10.020
<i>It's a well-balanced party!</i>

00:11:10.680 --> 00:11:11.860
We're all set, then.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:13.890
Let's take our party to the dungeon!

00:11:13.890 --> 00:11:15.020
Right!

00:11:18.710 --> 00:11:22.070
I had no idea there was a dungeon 
beneath the academy!

00:11:22.070 --> 00:11:24.750
Yes, the environmental features 
and monster strength

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:27.110
will differ floor by floor.

00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:30.210
The monsters on this floor 
shouldn't be particularly tough...

00:11:31.450 --> 00:11:32.960
I'll fetch one!

00:11:33.290 --> 00:11:35.000
Matty?

00:11:38.640 --> 00:11:39.600
Here!

00:11:40.220 --> 00:11:42.570
A monster!

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:44.940
Sorry to startle you.

00:11:44.940 --> 00:11:47.720
I figured we'd use it for practice.

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:52.640
Alma! Try to hit it 
with one of your arrows!

00:11:52.640 --> 00:11:53.770
Sure...

00:11:53.770 --> 00:11:58.190
But I don't think an arrow 
will get through that thing's shell.

00:11:58.190 --> 00:11:59.520
Just try it!

00:11:59.520 --> 00:12:01.920
Do what you'd do to fire off a spell,

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:03.740
but channel the magic 
into the arrow instead!

00:12:03.740 --> 00:12:05.140
Hm...

00:12:05.820 --> 00:12:06.990
Like this?

00:12:06.990 --> 00:12:10.000
Exactly! Now release the arrow!

00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:11.540
Here I go!

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:15.210
No way!

00:12:15.210 --> 00:12:16.940
That was incredible, Alma!

00:12:17.860 --> 00:12:20.910
That's the spell you used before, right?

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:23.760
Yeah, but that's just the first trick.

00:12:24.060 --> 00:12:27.620
Alma. This time, 
draw the bow and hold it.

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:28.390
Right!

00:12:30.250 --> 00:12:32.020
This time, after you release it,

00:12:32.020 --> 00:12:34.560
try to feel the connection 
between yourself and the arrow.

00:12:34.910 --> 00:12:37.040
It should feel like there's a thread 
of magic tied to the arrow,

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:40.000
and you're holding the other end.

00:12:41.220 --> 00:12:42.440
Like this?

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:44.780
Another monster!

00:12:45.820 --> 00:12:47.660
It changed course mid-flight!

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:50.370
That's called a Thread-Guided Enchant.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:55.950
Practice it until you can hit two monsters 
with one shot.

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:57.930
Okay, I'll try!

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:02.190
Monsters... Monsters...

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:04.310
Magistones will appear 
when you slay the monsters.

00:13:04.310 --> 00:13:07.390
Make sure you pick those up! 
We'll need them for the barrier!

00:13:07.390 --> 00:13:08.600
Got it!

00:13:08.600 --> 00:13:10.350
While she's gone, you and I will—

00:13:10.350 --> 00:13:12.200
Cast enchantments?!

00:13:12.200 --> 00:13:15.640
A-Actually, there's something else 
we need to do first.

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:16.940
Oh.

00:13:16.940 --> 00:13:20.320
Don't worry! 
It's part of learning enchantments!

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:23.030
Really?! I'll do my best!

00:13:26.220 --> 00:13:28.020
You'll want to learn 
how to make your own weapons

00:13:28.020 --> 00:13:30.540
so you'll have something 
to practice your enchantment spells on.

00:13:30.540 --> 00:13:33.620
Doesn't that take decades of training?

00:13:33.620 --> 00:13:35.570
They're just for practice purposes,

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:38.510
so you won't have 
to spend too long on them.

00:13:38.510 --> 00:13:41.150
Now, the raw material to make weapons...

00:13:41.150 --> 00:13:42.590
This should do.

00:13:44.540 --> 00:13:46.050
<i>Brittle Shatter.</i>

00:13:50.820 --> 00:13:52.650
This is crude dungeon ore.

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:56.490
We'll want to refine it 
to extract metal for the weapons.

00:13:56.490 --> 00:14:01.660
I thought dungeon walls were synonymous 
with indestructibility...

00:14:01.660 --> 00:14:05.340
They should be synonymous 
with valuable resources!

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:07.900
Anyway, let's refine it.

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:09.200
R-Right!

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:12.510
We'll use pure magic power 
to melt the dungeon ore,

00:14:12.510 --> 00:14:14.530
and a water spell to recrystallize it.

00:14:14.530 --> 00:14:16.930
Then we'll use a Brittle Shatter 
to smash those crystals into powder,

00:14:16.930 --> 00:14:19.680
followed by a magnet spell 
to aggregate the elements we want.

00:14:20.490 --> 00:14:23.240
We'll repeat this process 
again and again until...

00:14:23.240 --> 00:14:24.500
I did it!

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:26.880
Pure clusters of iron and mithril!

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:29.160
That was great for a first try!

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:30.650
Thank you!

00:14:30.650 --> 00:14:33.350
<i>And, wow... look at that smile!</i>

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:36.100
Will we use these 
to create weapons now?

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:37.250
Yes.

00:14:37.250 --> 00:14:39.250
You're such a fast learner.

00:14:39.250 --> 00:14:42.600
Let's see if we can go right 
from making a weapon to enchanting it!

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:43.660
Please!

00:14:46.810 --> 00:14:49.490
Yes! I can do three at once now!

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:53.450
I've gotten lots of magistones, 
so I'll head back and check in!

00:14:54.480 --> 00:14:57.550
Hope Lurie and Matty are getting along...

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:01.610
I did it!

00:15:01.610 --> 00:15:04.930
I enchanted the sword 
to let me break through walls!

00:15:06.020 --> 00:15:08.680
What in the world are they doing?

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:10.610
Awesome job, Lurie!

00:15:10.610 --> 00:15:12.890
You can make equipment already!

00:15:12.890 --> 00:15:13.870
Yes!

00:15:13.870 --> 00:15:16.350
But only because 
Matty is such a good teacher.

00:15:16.620 --> 00:15:19.770
Any monsters who come after us 
will regret it!

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:22.650
Yes, and we're hitting 
the tenth floor today.

00:15:22.650 --> 00:15:24.360
T-Tenth?!

00:15:24.360 --> 00:15:26.910
I think you can handle it.

00:15:26.910 --> 00:15:31.080
Let's use this as a test 
to see how much you've learned!

00:15:36.020 --> 00:15:40.080
This floor seems different 
from the previous ones...

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:41.160
Look! Look!

00:15:41.160 --> 00:15:43.000
Creepy!

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:45.630
I'll finish them 
with a wide-ranging fire attack spell!

00:15:48.480 --> 00:15:49.540
It didn't work?!

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:51.090
I'll try my arrows, then!

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:55.810
Yeah! A clean sweep!

00:15:55.810 --> 00:15:57.140
You're amazing, Alma!

00:16:03.560 --> 00:16:04.980
Stand back!

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:07.820
Hey, this one's pretty tough!

00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:09.520
I'll help you!

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:11.620
New arrows!

00:16:16.060 --> 00:16:17.590
Thanks, Lurie!

00:16:17.590 --> 00:16:18.330
Of course!

00:16:23.460 --> 00:16:27.250
<i>They're really getting the swing of combat.</i>

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:30.020
<i>My pendant consolidates the magic power 
of defeated monsters</i>

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:32.010
<i>to increase the experience points 
my party gains.</i>

00:16:32.010 --> 00:16:34.770
<i>It's playing a big part 
in their improvement, too!</i>

00:16:34.770 --> 00:16:37.160
<i>Great work, past me!</i>

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:42.660
<i>But the real test is coming up...</i>

00:16:42.660 --> 00:16:43.840
Be careful!

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:47.940
Killer Dogs are exponentially stronger 
than the monsters you've fought so far.

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:49.940
E-Exponentially?!

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:53.030
<i>Should I step in to save them?</i>

00:16:54.740 --> 00:16:55.780
Alma!

00:16:56.630 --> 00:16:58.090
Thanks, Lurie!

00:17:00.450 --> 00:17:01.750
And this should do it!

00:17:04.830 --> 00:17:05.740
Yes!

00:17:05.740 --> 00:17:06.790
Alma!

00:17:07.310 --> 00:17:09.000
Great work, you two!

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:13.000
Alma, you managed 
two simultaneous thread-guided arrows.

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:15.480
And Lurie, your support was amazing!

00:17:16.960 --> 00:17:20.160
It should be a while 
before more monsters come here.

00:17:20.160 --> 00:17:21.460
Let's set up a camp.

00:17:21.460 --> 00:17:22.560
A camp?

00:17:22.900 --> 00:17:25.690
A barrier to establish a safe area to rest.

00:17:25.990 --> 00:17:28.590
If I infuse this magistone 
with my magic power...

00:17:31.590 --> 00:17:33.060
There we go.

00:17:33.060 --> 00:17:34.780
Rest a while, you two.

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:36.500
Where are you going, Matty?

00:17:36.500 --> 00:17:38.950
To the lower floors.

00:17:38.950 --> 00:17:43.370
It's the only place to get 
the adamantite I need for the barrier.

00:17:43.770 --> 00:17:48.830
<i>And I'm ready to find out 
how far I've come.</i>

00:17:48.830 --> 00:17:51.550
How far down are you going to go?

00:17:51.550 --> 00:17:53.160
The twenty-fifth floor, I think?

00:17:53.160 --> 00:17:55.280
T-Twenty-fifth?!

00:17:55.280 --> 00:17:59.090
But the deepest anyone's ever gone 
in this dungeon is the twenty-third floor!

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:02.920
And that was the legendary thirty-man party

00:18:02.920 --> 00:18:05.630
under the protection 
of Gaius, God of Magic!

00:18:05.630 --> 00:18:08.920
<i>Did she just say, "Gaius, God of Magic"?</i>

00:18:09.440 --> 00:18:10.940
<i>A coincidence, perhaps?</i>

00:18:19.770 --> 00:18:23.200
<i>These weak monsters are a waste of my magic.</i>

00:18:23.510 --> 00:18:25.910
<i>I need to hurry to deeper floors!</i>

00:18:26.780 --> 00:18:27.550
There.

00:18:27.550 --> 00:18:30.420
The rocks here contain adamantite.

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:32.400
I'll gather it up and head back.

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:35.770
<i>This sensation...</i>

00:18:35.770 --> 00:18:37.130
<i>I'm sure of it.</i>

00:18:37.130 --> 00:18:38.990
<i>There's a powerful monster there...</i>

00:18:38.990 --> 00:18:40.890
<i>What's known as a floor boss.</i>

00:18:41.360 --> 00:18:44.970
<i>Floor bosses are the leading cause 
of party mortality.</i>

00:18:45.260 --> 00:18:50.140
<i>I currently have less magic power 
than the average mage from my past life.</i>

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:52.730
<i>What should I do under these circumstances?</i>

00:18:53.330 --> 00:18:55.570
<i>That's obvious, isn't it?</i>

00:18:56.140 --> 00:18:57.490
<i>I charge!</i>

00:18:57.490 --> 00:18:59.690
<i>I'll use all the knowledge, 
experience, and wits I possess</i>

00:18:59.690 --> 00:19:01.490
<i>to slay that floor boss!</i>

00:19:17.740 --> 00:19:20.270
<i>It's important the stage for your enemy.</i>

00:19:20.270 --> 00:19:22.660
<i>I've taken out all the monsters 
and pillars separating us</i>

00:19:22.660 --> 00:19:24.300
<i>and made it a path.</i>

00:19:24.300 --> 00:19:25.380
<i>Come to me...</i>

00:19:25.380 --> 00:19:26.510
<i>Compel Detect!</i>

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:30.340
<i>It's here?</i>

00:19:30.340 --> 00:19:32.310
<i>No, wait... It's—</i>

00:19:36.370 --> 00:19:39.800
Couldn't just use the path I made, 
could you?

00:19:40.390 --> 00:19:42.030
Arc Serpent...

00:19:43.530 --> 00:19:48.020
<i>One hit like that would be 
the death of me for sure.</i>

00:19:48.020 --> 00:19:49.290
<i>And not just that...</i>

00:19:49.610 --> 00:19:52.250
<i>Its venom corrodes the ground itself,</i>

00:19:52.250 --> 00:19:55.660
<i>and the fumes will toxify the air 
as time passes.</i>

00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:57.270
<i>I'll want to finish this quickly.</i>

00:19:57.830 --> 00:20:03.730
<i>But this will be my first proper challenge 
since acquiring the Fourth Crest...</i>

00:20:03.730 --> 00:20:05.320
Even if it won't last long,

00:20:05.320 --> 00:20:07.680
I fully intend to enjoy it!

00:20:09.520 --> 00:20:11.420
<i>A single scale?</i>

00:20:11.420 --> 00:20:13.980
<i>But that should be enough</i>

00:20:13.980 --> 00:20:15.830
<i>to make an opponent unaccustomed to injury</i>

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:18.640
<i>recognize me as a threat!</i>

00:20:21.270 --> 00:20:23.050
<i>As expected.</i>

00:20:29.500 --> 00:20:30.750
Was that painful?

00:20:31.280 --> 00:20:32.990
But it's not over yet...

00:20:33.960 --> 00:20:34.960
Sunder Steel!

00:20:34.960 --> 00:20:35.900
Resist Acid!

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:36.800
Magic Slash!

00:20:36.800 --> 00:20:37.980
Triple-cast!

00:20:45.400 --> 00:20:47.170
Still no effect?

00:20:47.170 --> 00:20:48.720
You're a real tough guy.

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:56.130
<i>Here's a little trick much loved 
by sword-wielding casters.</i>

00:20:56.970 --> 00:21:01.070
<i>The shattering of a magistone produces a thick veil 
of magic power and particles.</i>

00:21:01.070 --> 00:21:04.450
<i>I gather them all into my blade!</i>

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:11.410
<i>Special Magic Enchant!</i>

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:22.340
Wh-What was that? 
An earthquake?

00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:26.410
Erhard, did you feel 
a massive burst of magic?

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:27.760
Just your imagination.

00:21:27.760 --> 00:21:31.760
No human has power like that 
in this day and age.

00:21:32.530 --> 00:21:35.020
Welcome back, Matty!

00:21:35.020 --> 00:21:36.770
You're back sooner 
than I thought you'd be!

00:21:36.770 --> 00:21:41.570
Yeah, I beat a really big monster, 
and it kind of filled up my inventory.

00:21:41.570 --> 00:21:43.750
A really big monster?

00:21:43.750 --> 00:21:45.430
Yeah. See?

00:23:25.960 --> 00:23:27.800
Lurie! The demons are coming!

00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:28.940
Don't worry.

00:23:28.940 --> 00:23:31.420
We'll be safe if we stay 
in our camp and keep quiet!

00:23:31.420 --> 00:23:34.800
Well any barrier Matty's created would be—

00:23:34.800 --> 00:23:36.970
A-Are you...

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:38.420
No, Alma! Don't!

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:39.980
<b>Episode 3
The Strongest Sage Meets a Dragon.</b>

00:23:38.420 --> 00:23:39.930
Achoo!
